    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras enter May 31st with a focus on exploiting exploitable arms, headlined by **Junior Caminero** (75.43) and **Christian Yelich** (74.33). **Caminero** is our premier play, benefiting from a soft matchup against Kochanowicz (5.17 xERA) and an ideal spot in the fourth slot, where his dynamic platoon advantage should flourish. Similarly, **Yelich** thrives today due to the favorable platoon split and a top-of-the-order designation, effectively neutralizing the park factor concerns. We are also leaning heavily into **Colt Keith** (64.31) and **Casey Schmitt** (63.20); **Schmitt** is particularly intriguing as his score is bolstered by a high-advantage platoon matchup and a favorable wind forecast, combined with a slow opposing pitcher delivery that maximizes his stolen base potential\u2014a critical factor for our league\u2019s scarcity-driven strategy.\n\nOur most difficult decision of the day involved **Chase Meidroth**, who sat on the bubble with a 53.67 efficiency score. While **Meidroth** projected reasonably well against Montero, he was ultimately edged out of the utility and middle infield slots by the higher-upside profiles of **Kyle Schwarber** and **Caleb Durbin**, whose respective order and platoon adjustments provided greater ceiling potential. Risks remain centered on our elite bats; **Trea Turner** (52.46) and **Yordan Alvarez** (58.67) face formidable pitchers in Yamamoto and Misiorowski. **Turner** specifically deals with the double-edged sword of elite speed\u2014his ability to steal is mitigated by the pitcher's high hold rate, though we are banking on the favorable wind direction to carry a potential long ball. Meanwhile, **Lars Nootbaar** and **Hyeseong Kim** remain sidelined as we look to maximize our active game cap efficiency with the current lineup.",
